# The pin check is a composite action pinned to a commit in sasjs/utils, so a pull
# request cannot edit the checker it has to pass. What it can still edit is the
# workflow that invokes it - delete the step and the job never reports, which reads as
# a pass - so these paths need a maintainer's review.
#
# A file cannot enforce that on its own: pair this with a required status check on the
# "Action pins" job and a ruleset on the default branch. Until those exist, this is a
# request for review, not a block.
#
# Owners are the sasjs maintainers rather than one person, so a single absence does not
# hold the gate.
